        <div class="hidden" id="data-preloaded" data-preloaded="{&quot;topic_3269760&quot;:&quot;{\&quot;post_stream\&quot;:{\&quot;posts\&quot;:[{\&quot;id\&quot;:11652255,\&quot;name\&quot;:\&quot;frecklesnspectacles\&quot;,\&quot;username\&quot;:\&quot;frecklesnspectacles\&quot;,\&quot;avatar_template\&quot;:\&quot;/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/frecklesnspectacles/{size}/9078770_2.png\&quot;,\&quot;created_at\&quot;:\&quot;2024-11-22T23:00:23.239Z\&quot;,\&quot;cooked\&quot;:\&quot;\\u003cp\\u003eHi Everyone!\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eWe announced a lot of exciting updates as we gear up for Thanksgiving \\u003cimg src=\\\&quot;https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/turkey.png?v=12\\\&quot; title=\\\&quot;:turkey:\\\&quot; class=\\\&quot;emoji\\\&quot; alt=\\\&quot;:turkey:\\\&quot; loading=\\\&quot;lazy\\\&quot; width=\\\&quot;20\\\&quot; height=\\\&quot;20\\\&quot;\\u003e — Mesh and Image APIs available in published experiences, new Parental Controls to keep Roblox safe, sharing audio and video assets with your groups, and so much more!\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eThis recap brings together all of our announcements and updates from the Developer Forum into one convenient post. By doing so, we hope it’s easier for you to stay up-to-date on the latest news and developments from Roblox.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eRemember - we keep information at a high level within these recaps. For more information or to leave feedback, please comment on their official announcements linked below.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eLet’s dive in:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003chr\\u003e\\n\\u003ch2\\u003e\\n\\u003ca name=\\\&quot;betas-updates-1\\\&quot; class=\\\&quot;anchor\\\&quot; href=\\\&quot;#betas-updates-1\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003eBetas \\u0026amp; Updates\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/studio-beta-avatar-joint-upgrade-enabling-physically-simulated-characters/3266099\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e[Studio Beta] Avatar Joint Upgrade: Enabling Physically-Simulated Characters\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eWith this update, setting up physical avatar interactions, like ragdoll effects, becomes significantly easier.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eThis upgrade introduces force and torque-limited constraints directly into avatars, allowing you to create realistic, physics-driven movements effortlessly.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/client-beta-in-experience-mesh-image-apis-now-available-in-published-experiences/3267293\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e[Client Beta] In-experience Mesh \\u0026amp; Image APIs now available in published experiences\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eYou can now publish experiences with the \\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://create.roblox.com/docs/reference/engine/classes/EditableMesh\\\&quot;\\u003eEditableMesh \\u003c/a\\u003eand \\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://create.roblox.com/docs/reference/engine/classes/EditableImage\\\&quot;\\u003eEditableImage \\u003c/a\\u003eAPIs. With this update, we do not foresee any more breaking API changes and you can confidently publish experiences with these APIs.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003chr\\u003e\\n\\u003ch2\\u003e\\n\\u003ca name=\\\&quot;announcements-updates-2\\\&quot; class=\\\&quot;anchor\\\&quot; href=\\\&quot;#announcements-updates-2\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003eAnnouncements \\u0026amp; Updates\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/introducing-updates-to-our-safety-protections-and-parental-controls/3264200\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eIntroducing Updates to Our Safety Protections and Parental Controls\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eWe are introducing significant updates to the built-in protections for our youngest users and easy-to-use tools to give parents and caregivers more control and clarity.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eAs a reminder of our \\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/upcoming-changes-to-experience-guidelines/3070343\\\&quot;\\u003eJuly announcement\\u003c/a\\u003e, we are also updating our content access policies for users under 13. Users under the age of 9 will only be able to access experiences with a content label of “Minimal” or “Mild” by default.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eWe recently published \\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/updating-experience-guideline-policies-to-keep-our-younger-users-safe/3249079\\\&quot;\\u003eupdated policy guidance\\u003c/a\\u003e for our experience questionnaire to help keep our youngest users safe. Please remember to fill out the experience questionnaire for each of your experiences by December 3, 2024; otherwise, your experiences will not be accessible for users under 13. For more details, please refer to the “Next Steps” section.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eUsers under the age of 13 will no longer be able to directly message others on Roblox outside of games or experiences (also known as platform chat), and will need parental consent for direct messaging within experiences.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/now-live-update-your-genre-and-subgenre/3265896\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eNow Live! Update Your Genre and Subgenre\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eYou can view and update your experience’s genre and subgenre in Creator Hub.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eTrending experiences will also start to show up in Charts under genre-based sorts, such as “Trending in Puzzle”.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/moderation-notifications-appeals-in-studio/3267366\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eModeration Notifications \\u0026amp; Appeals in Studio\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eWe have released a small but important update to Studio that will let you know if your account has received a moderation warning or ban.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eOur intent is to offer a faster way to appeal incorrect moderations so you can quickly return to creation and development work.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/updating-touchswipe-introducing-touchdrag-next-week/3266901\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eUpdating TouchSwipe \\u0026amp; Introducing TouchDrag Next Week\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eTouchSwipe will behave consistently across all devices, and we’re adding a new TouchDrag API to support additional touch behaviors.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eIf you are currently using TouchSwipe within your experience, there is no work needed on your end; this update should be similar to a bug fix.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/review-your-generative-ai-data-sharing-preferences/3062106\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eReview Your Generative AI Data Sharing Preferences\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eUpdate: You no longer need to accept separate AI Supplemental Terms in Studio. We’ve integrated the AI Supplemental Terms into the \\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://en.help.roblox.com/hc/en-us/articles/115004647846-Roblox-Terms-of-Use\\\&quot;\\u003eRoblox Terms of Use\\u003c/a\\u003e and your continued use of our service is your agreement to these updated terms. You can still set your data-sharing preferences in Creator Hub and when publishing your experience.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/introducing-new-permissions-to-creator-group-roles/3268381\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eIntroducing New Permissions to Creator Group Roles\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eWe recently rolled out many new permissions for your Group roles created in Creator Hub.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eThis includes feature parity with many old permissions (such as avatar items, open cloud, and more), as well as some net new permissions around revenue management, assets, and experiences.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/introducing-roblox-communities/3268307\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eIntroducing Roblox Communities\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eRoblox Groups has been renamed to Roblox Communities.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eWe’re also introducing more capabilities for community admins and moderators with the highly requested Ban User feature, renaming the Exile User feature to Kick User, and updating the Open Cloud API.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/asset-privacy-and-permissions-share-audio-and-video-with-groups/3269446\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eAsset Privacy and Permissions: Share Audio and Video With Groups\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eYou can now share your private audio and video assets with your groups.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eGroup members can use the assets you share in any of the group’s experiences.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/platform-text-chat-is-coming-to-experiences/3223162\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003ePlatform Text Chat is coming to Experiences\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eUpdate: We’re rolling out Roblox Chat (platform chat) in experiences after the test we announced last month\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eAs part of this launch, we are introducing a new Roblox Chat icon across mobile, web, and desktop.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003eWe also heard your feedback and are returning to a modernized version of the Experience chat icon.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003chr\\u003e\\n\\u003ch2\\u003e\\n\\u003ca name=\\\&quot;release-notes-3\\\&quot; class=\\\&quot;anchor\\\&quot; href=\\\&quot;#release-notes-3\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003eRelease Notes\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/release-notes-for-652/3268227\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eRelease Notes for 652\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003chr\\u003e\\n\\u003ch2\\u003e\\n\\u003ca name=\\\&quot;deprecated-web-endpoints-4\\\&quot; class=\\\&quot;anchor\\\&quot; href=\\\&quot;#deprecated-web-endpoints-4\\\&quot;\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003eDeprecated Web Endpoints\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/official-list-of-deprecated-web-endpoints/62889/70\\\&quot;\\u003eOfficial List of Deprecated Web Endpoints\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003e\\n\\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/official-list-of-deprecated-web-endpoints/62889/80\\\&quot;\\u003eThis endpoint\\u003c/a\\u003e will be fully removed in the week of December 2nd. Most of the endpoint’s functionality has already been suspended.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003chr\\u003e\\n\\u003ch2\\u00